# Template for libbar.bst, rendered by examples/stage_project3_remote.sh
# by substituting @REMOTE_PATH@ - not a BuildStream project option
# (real constraint, confirmed via a real CI failure: BuildStream project
# options only support type: bool/enum/flags/element-mask/arch/os, no
# free-form string type to hold an arbitrary filesystem path), so this
# is templated the same way examples/stage_runtimes.sh and
# stage_project3_remote.sh already generate non-source content at build
# time rather than committing it.
#
# No `ref:` key deliberately - with ref-storage: project.refs, the
# resolved ref lives in project.refs, not in the element itself. `bst
# source track libbar.bst` (run by stage_project3_remote.sh's caller,
# see examples/README.md) resolves the real commit SHA from the
# generated remote and writes it there.
kind: import
sources:
- kind: git
  url: "file://@REMOTE_PATH@"
  track: main
